  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>First step of the reaction involves electrophilic addition of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Br</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>in</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mi>OH</mi></math>&nbsp;to&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>methyl</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>but</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>ene</mi><mo>&#160;</mo></math>to&nbsp;form A which contains an ether linkage.</p><p>A, undergoes cleavage reaction with HI&nbsp;by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></msub><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp;mechanism to form B as the major product as shown in the reactions below</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/a42af2ac-f2c6-4f08-85ef-139597ec0487-9757174_S.png\" style=\"width: 500px; height: 257px;\" /></p></blockquote>",
